title: $:/plugins/nikorion/dyntable/language/lingo
tags: $:/tags/Global

<!--
table wikitext i18n. Two separate entry points, on purpose.

Why two and not one: in TiddlyWiki, "render wikitext" and "return a string" are
two distinct, non-interchangeable mechanisms.
  - `dyntable-lingo` (\procedure) → RENDERS the wikitext (widgets: backticks
    → <code>, clickable links, etc.). Use it in a tiddler body / for prose.
  - `dyntable-lingo-text` (\function) → returns a RAW string (unrendered).
    The only form that can be dropped into an attribute (tooltip=<<…>>), a !!
    heading, or inline HTML where a <p> would get in the way. Does not
    render wikitext.
A \procedure cannot serve as an attribute value (its body is a widget, not a
string); a \function cannot render wikitext. Hence both.

Why the lang→en-GB→key fallback is repeated in each rather than factored into a
shared helper \function: a custom \function called as a direct filter operator
(`[my-fn<arg>]`) does NOT bind its operand to the parameter in TW 5.4 — it
silently yields nothing. Factoring the cascade out therefore breaks resolution
entirely. Also note the strings are SHADOW tiddlers (packaged in the plugin),
so existence must be tested with `get[text]`, never `is[tiddler]`/`!is[missing]`
(which match real, non-shadow tiddlers only).
So the cascade stays inline, duplicated across the definitions below.

A third entry point, `dyntable-lingo-value` (\function), translates a DATA value
(column name, node type…) rather than a UI key: same lang→en-GB cascade
under `<prefix><value>`, but its final fallback is the raw value itself, not
the key. So an untranslated value — a user's own field, say — displays as
is. Call it through the `function` operator, which does bind its operands:
`[function[dyntable-lingo-value],[Tables/Column/],<currentColumn>]`.
-->

\procedure dyntable-lingo(title)
\whitespace trim
<$let _prefix="$:/plugins/nikorion/dyntable/language/"
      _lang={{{ [[$:/language]get[text]get[name]] }}}
      _suffix={{{ [[/]addsuffix<title>] }}}
      _key={{{ [<_lang>addprefix<_prefix>addsuffix<_suffix>] }}}>
<%if [<_key>get[text]] %>
<$transclude $tiddler=<<_key>>/>
<%else%>
<$transclude $tiddler={{{ [[en-GB]addprefix<_prefix>addsuffix<_suffix>] }}}/>
<%endif%>
</$let>
\end

\function dyntable-lingo-text(title)
[[$:/language]get[text]get[name]else[en-GB]] [[en-GB]]
+[addprefix[$:/plugins/nikorion/dyntable/language/]] +[addsuffix[/]]
+[addsuffix<title>] 
+[get[text]] +[limit[1]]
:else[<title>]
\end

\function dyntable-lingo-value(prefix, value)
[[$:/language]get[text]get[name]else[en-GB]] [[en-GB]]
+[addprefix[$:/plugins/nikorion/dyntable/language/]] +[addsuffix[/]]
+[addsuffix<prefix>] +[addsuffix<value>] 
+[get[text]] +[limit[1]]
:else[<value>]
\end
